From 4199bc19c5eac6fcb88dc454f06c0afdda6ba0f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charles Hoskinson <charles.hoskinson@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:07:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] E4: GPU Merkle hashing hooks for the Fr config,
 deterministic grind

MerkleHasher gets has_batch, hash_rows, encode_hash_rows and digest_layers
(default None); cpu-backend RS encode, digest layers, the WHIR tree and the
reference MerkleTree::new call them first. FrMerkleHasher implements them under
the stark-sdk feature gpu with mori-gpu (Midnight Poseidon over Fr and the
sppark NTT); MORI_GPU=off takes the CPU path. The PoW grind searches ordered
chunks with find_first, so a proof is reproducible at any thread count (two
20-thread proofs differed with find_any). The L_Fr GPU proof is byte-identical
to the CPU proof.
